corrected:
1) Required in the same change: suppress the ghost click.
- In src/ui/project/Viewer.tsx (the effect around lines 183-257), add `cv.addEventListener('touchend', e => e.preventDefault(), { passive: false })` and remove it in the cleanup. The canvas already has touch-action:none and only pointer events drive pan, pinch and pick, so nothing else changes.
- Let `pointercancel` only clear the pointer state; it should not run the pick logic in onUp.
- Optional extra safety in src/ui/components.tsx Modal: ignore clicks inside `.modal` for 300 ms after mount.
- Add an e2e touch test: open a context with hasTouch, tap the canvas, and assert that the stone colour and the 'stone-placed' checkbox did not change and that stone-id equals the tapped cell.

2) Touch sizing at the end of src/ui/styles.css:
```css
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  .btn, .btn.small, .btn.chip, .segmented button, .neighbor, select, input.text, .numin input { min-height: 44px }
  .legend-item, .section-cell { min-height: 40px }
  .icon-btn, .viewer-tools button { min-width: 44px; min-height: 44px }
  .step { min-height: 44px }
  .cp { min-width: 44px; min-height: 48px }
  input[type=range] { height: 36px }
  .numin input, select, input.text { font-size: 16px }
  label.inline input[type=checkbox] { width: 22px; height: 22px }
}
```
- Keep the native range thumb; skip `::-webkit-slider-thumb`.
- Raise the NumberInput widths in StoneDialog (56) and FreeformEditor (60) to about 72 px under coarse pointers so values stay readable at 16 px.

3) Stone dialog at 600 px or narrower: reorder it instead of using tabs, so every requirement-13 detail stays mounted and e2e/run-e2e.cjs keeps working. Order:
- (a) A sticky compact summary in the modal body: ID, swatch, code and name, W×H mm, shape, and the "dieser Stein ist verlegt" checkbox as a label at least 44 px tall.
- (b) "Farbe ändern": the 12 colours with the smallest ΔE in one horizontally scrollable row, plus an "Alle Farben" button that expands the full sorted list (currently `similar.slice(0, 40)`).
- (c) Cut instructions and CutTemplateSvg, unchanged: same analyzeCut output, no new numbers.
- (d) Form ändern.
- (e) Position, coordinates, section, and the neighbour buttons. Keep these for navigation; no extra prev/next arrows.
- Optionally style the modal as a bottom sheet (`.modal-backdrop{align-items:flex-end;padding:0}`, `.modal{border-radius:16px 16px 0 0; padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom)}`) only on narrow screens.
- Ship this only together with step 1. The bottom sheet and colour-first layout raise the share of ghost clicks that hit editing controls (measured 12-25 of 39 taps recoloured stones without the fix, 0 with it).
